mantle rm523
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_hollis_slagwick
title the wooden window
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk looks_through_a_small_carved_frame_before_choosing_a_view
likes blackberries whittling festival_bells summer_evenings
dislikes stale_bread rats
fears a_wet_wall_hidden_behind_a_fine_prospect
hopes a_high_window_shared_with_a_trusted_wolf
topics home +0.6 pastimes +0.5 dreams +0.3 work +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=measured tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# frames a narrow view in a rectangle of carved wood, setting it down whenever damp air catches in the throat.

words
oath! = Four damp corners | My missing shutter
saying! = Frame the view yourself | Check the inner sill
framebit = a pocket window | my little rectangle
deepedge = a slim bevel | the shadow edge
burrchip = a rough corner | the last splinter
glassnone = the open pane | my empty glazing
windowleg = a carved upright | the narrow jamb
berrydot = a purple spot | the berry stain
clapper = a far bell note | the little chime
drythroat = a bad catch | my dry pause
sillview = a long prospect | the upper view
lowplaster = a damp patch | the low stain
boardfloor = a straight board | the clear floor
daylightbar = a slant of light | the pale opening

any
opinion houses mixed 0 : A fine window shows excellent taste. Where the servants sleep may show a truer account of the household.
opinion city for 1 : A clear evening can give me the same distant hill from half a dozen different ranks of windows.
opinion merchants against 1 : I'd inspect the frame underneath the paint before accepting anybody's price for polish.
opinion strangers against 1 : I'd rather choose what comes into my room than leave my door to public taste.
opinion road mixed 0 : A good view of a lane doesn't show whether its drains work.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : Give me the bells heard at a civil distance and somebody else may take my place in the crowd.

grown
line greet : Hello. Stand outside the frame for a moment. | Welcome. You've caught a clear patch.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new face in this narrow prospect. | You can speak by this close corner of my sill.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning gives the carving a clean edge. | Light from the east fits this opening neatly.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. The frame can go in my pocket. | My attention is off the sill now.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A known face improves an ordinary view. | You're welcome within my little rectangle.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : Evening. Dark begins in the corners. | There's enough left in the opening for two voices.
line again.open : Back inside the view again. | I've shifted the frame since we spoke.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come see a whole roof fitted in here! | Take this exact angle before the light goes!
line farewell : May your room have an honest window. | A smooth latch at your destination.
line farewell.return : I'll put away my little view now. | Go before the light leaves that jamb altogether.
line react.news : Tell me what actually stood inside your view. | A narrow account with the edges known will suit me.
line react.news.new : That hasn't come through my opening before. | A fresh shape for the little frame.
line react.news.known : It was in the earlier account's field as well. | I've seen that outline in a previous telling.
line react.news.doubt : A great deal appears to be happening outside the stated view. | I'd check what the frame cuts off there.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Sit clear of every watching window. | I can spare you somebody peering at a hard moment.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : A fine bit of fortune inside one day's frame. | Glad news gives a dark pane some useful light.
line ask.how : Does today give you a tolerable outlook? | Any clear patch ahead of your errands?
line answer.how : Managing. My wood has a slight catch, that's all. | Fairly comfortable in this light.
line decline : That would open a part of my day kept for home. | I haven't had that view myself and can't vouch for it.
line accept_decline : Then I'll leave your shutter drawn. | Very well. A plain edge to the matter.
line preclose : Time I put the frame back in its wrapping. | My next household duty is coming into view.
line accept_preclose : Go while the light still serves you. | We'll leave the opening clear for another time.
line thank : You brought the real corner into view. Thank you. | I appreciate a kindness offered without inspection.
line deflect_thanks : I merely shifted a narrow bit of wood. | It took very little of my available light.
line sympathise : One can draw a curtain when a day is cruel. | There's room outside other wolves' gaze over here.
line reassure : Try a smaller opening till the whole view seems manageable. | No need to display what you're still mending.
line ack : I see the actual corner now. | That puts the right part in view.
line give.advice : View a promising room with every shutter open. | A polished sill may have damp under its lip.

scene carve
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This scrap has a rectangle where a knot fell out. I carved the edges till it became a travelling window.
b : Does it magnify a hill? | Why leave the hole empty?
a : No. It just puts an end to the rest of the landscape. Occasionally a great improvement. | A little glass would add glare and weight. I want the hole to do the viewing.

scene lowbirth
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The rooms I knew in the Sump had windows that admitted a great deal besides the outlook.
b : Water, you mean? | Would a higher floor have helped?
a : Water and remarks from the street. Neither asked whether the room was ready. | With the water. For the remarks I'd prefer a good thickness of wall.

scene highwish
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I measure a high room in private, holding the window to the sky above a low roof.
b : What would go below it? | Would you always keep it open?
a : A dry bed. After that I'd consider a chair and what the view might be worth. | Only when the weather justified the opening. A fine prospect needn't be allowed to soak my floor.

scene service
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I begin a household task by looking at the space someone else needs after I've gone.
b : Can a clear space be work? | Who notices the result?
a : A tray set out of the passage can be worth more than another ten minutes of polishing. | Ordinary arrangements suit me. Nobody should need to stop and work out what I meant.

scene learner
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning how a household's working day looks once a door opens inward.
b : Can't you just walk through? | What's different there?
a : I'd rather understand whose work I'd interrupt first. A learner can afford to wait at the jamb. | Usually the light and the number of things a pair of arms can reach. Both matter in actual service.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd share a high window with #self.spouse# before I'd show it to any curious visitor.
b : Which side would you take? | Is that the reason for wanting one?
a : Whichever leaves both chairs with a decent outlook. I can give that some thought before we move. | One reason. A good private room ought to belong to the lives actually lived inside it.

scene berry
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stain one corner of my frame with a blackberry. It's how I tell the side that goes toward my eyes.
b : Doesn't it stay sticky? | Could you use a notch instead?
a : Only a thin stain after I've finished eating the berry. It dries on my sill. | I could. The berry gives me a good reason to stop and eat something I like.

scene rasp
when topic=health here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Damp gives my voice a rough grain. I put the carving down a moment when that happens.
b : Is the wood to blame? | Would you like some quiet?
a : I prefer to discuss the grain in the frame. It can stand being inspected. | For the length of one comfortable breath. Then we can carry on as usual.

scene summer
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Summer evening has just the light I want to keep inside the frame.
b : What colour suits the frame? | Can you hold it steady?
a : The pale band above the darkest roof. The colours need each other to look right. | With my elbow against a dry jamb. Several fairly modest things make possible a comfortable view.

scene bells
when topic=festival self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bright bell note travels farther than a festival banner can be seen. I can frame the source in an empty sky.
b : Why watch an empty square? | Would you rather be at the bell?
a : It's a pleasure to have a private little piece of all that noise. | No. I like the sound after it's lost the sharp part and found a useful distance.

scene bread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale crust scrapes where damp has already caught my throat. I wait for something warm to take with it.
b : Would broth do? | Why keep the crust?
a : Very well. Then the two can make a meal together without an argument. | Bread has a cost. My preference for a smooth swallow won't bring back the money.

scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Put berries in a covered dish. A rat doesn't need a grand prospect to find a supper.
b : Does a high shelf work? | Could you leave it by the frame?
a : A tight cover works better. I'd give a rat credit for knowing how to climb. | My carved window is remarkably deficient as a barrier. Air and appetites can both get through.

scene working
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An Office quarter window can show a great deal of paper moving without showing a decision.
b : Do you watch often? | Would you take a desk there?
a : Only in passing. I've plenty to form an opinion of this side of my particular pane. | I'd ask what the duties involve first. A comfortable seat scarcely makes a trade worth learning.

scene quietfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In prayer I picture a clear opening with room for one honest hope. A very small frame is enough.
b : Does the hope need words? | Which way does it face?
a : A few. I'd rather make the request plainly than bury it in grand scenery. | Toward the Bright One. The wood is just how my hands remember to hold still.

scene shopview
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I'd price a room in hard rain and again when dry. The second price owes the first an explanation.
b : Would a fine view count? | What about a little drip?
a : After the bedding stays dry, yes. One can spend a handsome rent on a poor night's sleep. | A drip over empty paving is weather. A drip through my blanket is a faulty room.

scene friendhush
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : With #self.friend# I can put the little frame down and let an evening look after itself.
b : Do you usually need it? | Would you lend it?
a : No. I enjoy choosing the view. With good company I can let the whole prospect come at once. | If I trusted the hand. A fragile corner ought to be returned still fit for viewing.

scene heardnews
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard the following from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. I'm keeping the source inside the frame.
b : Are the edges certain? | Would you act upon that?
a : The edges of what I heard, yes. A view from the actual spot might include things I don't know. | I'd want an account from nearer the event if any household depended on my decision.

scene crookwall
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crooked jamb looks straight if I turn the little frame far enough. A comforting trick with very limited uses.
b : When would you use it? | What's the limit?
a : To see how a line might look after proper repair. Imagination has its legitimate employments. | I still have to shut the actual window. The latch has never shown any interest in my opinion.

grown

story berrypane [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I used a blackberry to mark the inside of my frame and a damp thumb to turn it round. Marked all four corners in short order.
  : For a day I owned a very superior window with no outside at all.
  b : How did you settle its direction?
  : Cut a tiny groove in one stained corner. I prefer berries in a bowl now.

story wetview [topic=home|memories]
  : A clear opening above a lengthy stairway once seemed to show a beautiful blue hillside. I took two extra steps to see it better.
  : A blue apron had been hung across the outside. The hill was a crease in the cloth.
  b : Was there a view behind it?
  : A perfectly serviceable brick wall. The hill wanted a little more laundry, not a more fortunate tenant.

story lastbell [topic=festival|memories]
  : I held the frame around a patch of sky while the last festival bell sounded. Lowered it when the note ran out.
  : There was another little note quite near my hand. My own metal button had caught on the wooden edge.
  b : Did you take an encore?
  : I freed the button. A household servant is entitled to one accidental performance per evening.

rule @corners
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hold it level. The roof will supply its own slope. | Fine prospect through one empty scrap.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Put the tray where the door can clear its corner. | Let the household have all the walking room past that doorway.

rule @damp
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A moment for this rough grain to settle. | Damp air has given that last syllable an extra edge.

rule @berry
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A purple spot to mark my frame's inner lip. | Blackberries in a covered dish will last till supper.

dlg resident.hub : I've put the wooden window aside. What would you like brought into view?
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you still fit our last comfortable angle of conversation.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : After dark the rectangle shows mostly lantern light. I can spare it a while.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : A short clear question from your side of this carving, please.
dlg resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I keep the household's actual work in view while the finer prospect takes care of itself.
dlg resident.job : I'm interested in duties whose boundaries can be stated before the day begins.
dlg resident.bye : May the far wall of your room stay dry in every weather.

graft resident.hub
choice Let me look through your wooden window. -> lookthrough
node lookthrough
say Hold it closer for a broad prospect. At arm's length you can fit the highest corner of one roof exactly inside. For a moment that's your room's view.
free
choice And what do you imagine behind the window? -> backroom
choice I'll take the wide prospect for now. -> hub
node backroom
say Dry plaster, a sound sill and two chairs with equal claims on the light. Rank comes well behind those on my list of desirable fittings.
choice I see why you left the frame empty. -> hub
choice I'll find my own view. -> bye
